    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass, including every checkpoint touching the redesigned identity.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'` and dropped sequence numbers. All changes were in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the mapper needed no change \u2014 it derives everything from `customerCode`).\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Replaced the `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` sequence-based builder with `customerCode(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)`, which produces `region + \"-\" + hash8(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- Added `hash8(input)` \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256.\n- Added `deriveRegion(postcode, city)` \u2014 postcode-range lookup first (NSW/VIC/QLD), city-table fallback, then `UNKNOWN`; mirrors the mapper's `locality` derivation so the code's region and the owner's locality always agree.\n- The create call now uses the normalized telephone and the owner's postcode/city/last name.\n\n**Why nothing else needed edits** \u2014 everything downstream already derives from `customerCode`:\n- Membership number (`<code>-M<YY>`) and its Luhn check digit are computed from `customerCode` in the mapper and automatically reflect the new value.\n- The audit line already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now carries the region-and-hash code.\n- Locality is unchanged and still returns the region (Cp17 confirms `NSW`).\n\nThe audit log confirms real values like `NSW-779D69B5` and `UNKNOWN-B7B77DD7`. Full suite: **45 tests, 0 failures**.",
